From db5e466d3c3816f2cac627ca66cea9c6734f7ecc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicandros Nic <nicandris@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 16:07:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] greeter: Stop the notification timer when a PAM message
 arrives
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

notificationResetTimer is started by onLoginFailed and is only ever
stopped by firing. If PAM sends an information message while that 3
second timeout is still pending — a retry after a failed attempt, where
pam_u2f's "cue" asks for a touch again — the timer fires and clears the
cue the user is still acting on.

Stop the timer before showing the message, so it lives until
handleLoginRequest() clears it on the next attempt, as intended.

CCBUG: 513560
---
 src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml b/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
index e4891dfb..ae440c0d 100644
--- a/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
+++ b/src/frontend/greeter/qml/Main.qml
@@ -372,6 +372,8 @@ Item {
         // e.g. pam_u2f's "cue" asking the user to touch their key. Not auto-cleared
         // like "Login Failed" is: handleLoginRequest() clears it on the next attempt.
         function onInformationMessage(message) {
+            // A reset pending from an earlier failure would clear this one early.
+            notificationResetTimer.stop();
             notificationMessage = message;
         }
 
